-- title:
--   Rankin-mass bound for canonical carry truncation
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be finite, let $k,W,b$ be natural numbers, let $N\ge1$ and $R\ge2$ be integers, and let $\chi$ be a smooth sieve cutoff. Fix CFZ forms $(L_q)_{q\in\kappa}$ and real frequencies $t,u\in\mathbb R^\kappa$. Their canonical carry-truncation discrepancy satisfies
--   $$
--   \|\Delta_{N,\chi,W,b,R,L}(t,u)\|\le\mathcal M_{N,W,b,R,L}\,D_{\chi,0}(t)D_{\chi,0}(u).
--   $$
--   Here $\mathcal M$ is the canonical carry-truncation Rankin mass, retaining its actual Rankin weights, and $D_{\chi,0}$ is the Fourier product-moment density with all moment orders zero.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/Sieve/CFZCanonicalDivisorRankinTruncation.lean#L462-L535

